      "articleId": "effaefb9090bc3b0e884",
      "headline": "National Consultations Chronogramme Puts 2027 Elections Under Pressure",
      "dek": "The timeline for national consultations, meant to inform a new constitution, may delay critical 2027 elections, including the presidential vote.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Madagascar's national consultation process, intended to lay the groundwork for a new constitution, faces a critical timeline challenge. The resolutions from these consultations are not expected until after May 2027, the same period slated for a constitutional referendum or election. This compressed schedule leaves little time for drafting a new constitution and organizing a vote, potentially impacting the entire 2027 electoral calendar.",
        "The process, officially launched after several postponements, involves training facilitators and conducting consultations at various administrative levels from September to November. The national consultation phase itself is scheduled between March and May 2027. A committee of experts will then need to transform the consultation outcomes into a constitutional text, followed by procedures for adoption and the organization of elections, including the presidential vote due by the end of 2027.",
        "Authorities maintain the schedule is feasible, with plans for parallel workstreams on electoral governance and preparations not dependent on consultation outcomes. The Prime Minister has reaffirmed government support, with a technical committee to manage the process. The core challenge remains synchronizing the conclusion of consultations, the establishment of a new constitution, and the organization of both the constitutional vote and the presidential election before the December 2027 deadline."
      ],
      "body": "Madagascar's national consultation process, intended to lay the groundwork for a new constitution, faces a critical timeline challenge. The resolutions from these consultations are not expected until after May 2027, the same period slated for a constitutional referendum or election. This compressed schedule leaves little time for drafting a new constitution and organizing a vote, potentially impacting the entire 2027 electoral calendar.\n\nThe process, officially launched after several postponements, involves training facilitators and conducting consultations at various administrative levels from September to November. The national consultation phase itself is scheduled between March and May 2027. A committee of experts will then need to transform the consultation outcomes into a constitutional text, followed by procedures for adoption and the organization of elections, including the presidential vote due by the end of 2027.\n\nAuthorities maintain the schedule is feasible, with plans for parallel workstreams on electoral governance and preparations not dependent on consultation outcomes. The Prime Minister has reaffirmed government support, with a technical committee to manage the process. The core challenge remains synchronizing the conclusion of consultations, the establishment of a new constitution, and the organization of both the constitutional vote and the presidential election before the December 2027 deadline.",
